From: =?UTF-8?q?Miroslav=20Mr=C3=A1z?= <mraz.miro@seznam.cz>
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 22:27:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7150-google-sunfish: link
 touchscreen to panel
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Pixel 4a's FTM5 touch IC is bonded into the Samsung OLED panel
module; the touch chip's analog power comes from the panel's own
VSP/VSN rails, not from the regulators the stmfts driver itself votes
on. Link the touchscreen node to the sofef00 panel via the standard
"panel" phandle so stmfts can register as a drm_panel_follower and
power-cycle the chip in lockstep with the display.

Before this, the chip silently lost power on every screen blank and
came back uninitialised on screen wake — touch was dead until an i2c
rebind. With the follower link the framework's prepare/unprepare
brackets the chip's lifecycle correctly and touch survives screen
blank/wake cycles.

Signed-off-by: Miroslav Mráz <mraz.miro@seznam.cz>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-google-sunfish.dts | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-google-sunfish.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-google-sunfish.dts
index cf3acf2b9010..5d67dd9b0dc7 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-google-sunfish.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-google-sunfish.dts
@@ -580,6 +580,20 @@ touchscreen@49 {
 		interrupts-extended = <&tlmm 9 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
 		reset-gpios = <&tlmm 8 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 
+		/*
+		 * The FTM5 touch IC is in-cell — it physically lives inside
+		 * the OLED panel module and is powered through the panel's
+		 * own VSP/VSN rails. The driver therefore registers as a DRM
+		 * panel follower so that stmfts_power_on() / _off() are
+		 * driven by the panel's prepare / unprepare callbacks. When
+		 * the screen blanks, the panel cuts power to the chip; on
+		 * unblank the driver re-runs the SYSTEM_RESET / SLEEP_OUT /
+		 * tuning / calibration sequence so scan mode actually
+		 * resumes (without this hook, the chip silently halts after
+		 * the first display blank).
+		 */
+		panel = <&panel>;
+
 		/*
 		 * GPIO 72 routes the touch IRQ between the AP (active-low)
 		 * and SLPI (active-high). Mainline only services the AP path,
